.TH "GEOLOCATIONPOSITION.TOJSON" "3JS" "October 30, 2026" "JavaScript" "JavaScript Reference Manual"
.SH NAME
GeolocationPosition.toJSON \- GeolocationPosition: toJSON() method
.SH SYNOPSIS
The \f[B]\f[CB]toJSON()\f[B]\f[R] method of the
\f[CR]GeolocationPosition\f[R] interface returns a JSON\-serializable
plain object representing the \f[CR]GeolocationPosition\f[R] object.
.PP
The method is automatically called by \f[CR]JSON.stringify()\f[R] when a
\f[CR]GeolocationPosition\f[R] object is encountered during JSON
serialization.
.SH SYNTAX
.IP
.EX
toJSON()
.EE
.SS Parameters
None.
.SS Return value
A JSON\-serializable plain object containing the following properties:
.IP \(bu 2
\f[CR]timestamp\f[R]
.IP \(bu 2
\f[CR]coords\f[R]
.PP
Each property\(cqs value is copied as\-is.
When the returned object is passed to \f[CR]JSON.stringify()\f[R], the
\f[CR]coords\f[R] property is further serialized using
\f[CR]GeolocationCoordinates.toJSON()\f[R].
.SH EXAMPLES
.SS Calling toJSON() directly
This example obtains a \f[CR]GeolocationPosition\f[R] object.
Calling \f[CR]toJSON()\f[R] directly returns a plain object.
Its properties have the same values as the corresponding properties of
the original object.
.IP
.EX
navigator.geolocation.getCurrentPosition((position) \f[B]=>\f[R] {
  \f[B]const\f[R] json = position.toJSON();
  console.log(json); \f[I]// A plain object\f[R]
  console.log(\f[B]typeof\f[R] json); \f[I]// \(dqobject\(dq\f[R]
  console.log(json.timestamp); \f[I]// Same value as position.timestamp\f[R]
});
.EE
.SS Serializing to a JSON string
Within the callback from the previous example, the same object can be
serialized using \f[CR]JSON.stringify()\f[R], which calls the
\f[CR]toJSON()\f[R] method automatically.
.IP
.EX
console.log(JSON.stringify(position));
.EE
.PP
This would log a JSON string like so (formatted for readability):
.IP
.EX
{
  \(dqtimestamp\(dq: 1717509611840,
  \(dqcoords\(dq: {
    \(dqaccuracy\(dq: 13.5,
    \(dqlatitude\(dq: 53.125,
    \(dqlongitude\(dq: 8.75,
    \(dqaltitude\(dq: \f[B]null\f[R],
    \(dqaltitudeAccuracy\(dq: \f[B]null\f[R],
    \(dqheading\(dq: \f[B]null\f[R],
    \(dqspeed\(dq: \f[B]null\f[R]
  }
}
.EE
.SH SEE ALSO
.IP \(bu 2
\f[CR]JSON\f[R]
